{"kind":"request","text":"Give durable statements a commit-style title/body presentation and a read-only Inspect dialog. Treat the first line of signed statement text as its title and the remaining paragraphs as its body without changing the durable schema; move request conditions of satisfaction into an accessible centered inspector opened from the row's hover controls.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-durable-title-inspector","conditions":"The signed record schema and exact text bytes remain unchanged; for display, the first non-empty line of statement.text is the title and text after the separating newline is the body; legacy single-line statements render correctly; paragraph breaks and long words are handled safely; work cards lead with the title and do not dump long bodies or conditions into the scan path; the selected thread presents title and body with a clear readable hierarchy; a read-only Inspect control is available alongside other non-mutating row controls and before a visible divider separating controls that append durable acts; Inspect opens a viewport-centered accessible dialog with focus containment/restoration, Escape and explicit close behavior, responsive sizing, and internal scrolling; for requests the dialog labels and displays the complete conditions of satisfaction at normal readable size, together with enough compact identity to know which durable item is inspected; opening or closing Inspect changes no durable or personal workroom state; no conditions are hidden solely in a hover tooltip; request-authoring guidance adopts a concise first-line title, blank line, explanatory body convention while keeping observable conditions in body.conditions; #2524 and representative single-line, multiline, long-condition, and non-request statements are regression cases; UI tests cover parsing, rendering, dialog accessibility, control grouping, and absence of mutations; the embedded UI is rebuilt; relevant documentation is updated with correct behavioral provenance; relevant UI and Go gates pass; an independent agent approves the exact implementation head before merge.","priority":"usability-feature","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}